Description: Spatial analyses involving binning require that every bin have the
    same area, but this is impossible using a rectangular grid laid over the
    Earth or over any projection of the Earth. Discrete global grids use
    hexagons, triangles, and diamonds to overcome this issue, overlaying the
    Earth with equally-sized bins. This package provides utilities for working
    with discrete global grids, along with utilities to aid in plotting such data.
